ayload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a51e6cbfe3f6b7f66b3c7e5a28a411dfdeb62ff6d2b8a37dbd05f0d5f57f5893","event_uuid":"689d2d8a-07ad-45b1-8989-0660404c10e6","position":{"commit_sha":"27936611c7a9a5927fce8a2a469db810e5b641f8","position":"1786451800726104001-689d2d8a-07ad-45b1-8989-0660404c10e6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a74ecda1fb43a02437f661386b6ace44ba779ea9a7d0ab9388997c6cd6c17beb","event_uuid":"111708ec-0eb2-4f22-a1f4-e7a2eec57892","position":{"commit_sha":"42bc46ddc4ba62cf5793300156b3873783003d92","position":"1786452161492595001-111708ec-0eb2-4f22-a1f4-e7a2eec57892"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Confirmed RCA: tests/_stall_remote.py sends one fixed rate//10 chunk per loop, so delayed 0.1-second wake-ups permanently reduce actual throughput below the rate promised by the fixture. With forced 0.55-second wake-ups, real Git reported the 1000 B/s low-speed abort in 2/2 trials while every send gap stayed below 0.56 seconds; cumulative elapsed-time pacing held about 4000 B/s and returned only the expected malformed-protocol failure in 2/2. The defect is test-only: production floor/window values remain correct and unchanged.","timestamp":1786447075918577001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA refinement: cumulative pacing fixes repeated late wake-ups but cannot recover after libcurl has already aborted during one uninterrupted scheduling gap. Controlled pauses confirmed the configured low-speed window is the boundary, so the stable remedy splits fast zero-byte stall controls from one production-window dribble integration and tests pacing math deterministically.","timestamp":1786451800726104001}],"created_at":1786445637061034001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"614919e9-5f1f-4faf-8a81-d0fb0bedfac1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"521b-04c3-572f-4514"}],"description":"## Context\n\nA 40-minute full suite intermittently classifies the shared dribbling fake remote as stalled. The unchanged test passes in isolation. The helper sends rate // 10 bytes per nominal 0.1-second wake-up, so delayed wake-ups reduce cumulative throughput. A cumulative catch-up fix removes that drift, but a full-suite experiment still produced one uninterrupted gap long enough to trip the artificial 2-second window. Production intentionally uses a 10-second window and must not change.\n\n## Proven root cause\n\nThe tests apply the same artificial 2-second window to zero-byte positive controls and above-floor negative controls. Libcurl correctly aborts any sufficiently long no-byte interval, so a scheduler-delayed Python fixture cannot make the negative control deterministic. Runtime experiments showed a 4-second pause trips a 2-second window, a 2.5-second pause does not trip a 10-second window, and a 10.5-second pause trips the 10-second window.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Extract the helper's cumulative bytes-owed calculation and prove delayed wake-up catch-up with a pure deterministic unit test.\n2. Keep the 2-second window only for zero-byte stall tests at every wrapper surface.\n3. Keep one real Git/libcurl above-floor negative control at the shared snapshot boundary, using the production 10-second window and a transfer long enough to cross it.\n4. Remove redundant live dribble timing trials at wrapper call sites; their existing argv tests already prove each wrapper installs the shared low-speed configuration.\n5. Run both consumer modules and the full suite. Verify src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py has no diff.\n\nThis follows the common layered-test pattern: deterministic mechanism coverage, one integration contract at the shared boundary, and per-caller wiring tests.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A pure test proves cumulative bytes owed equals floor(rate * elapsed) minus bytes already sent after a delayed wake-up.\n- [ ] Every zero-byte stall case still fails specifically as a stall under the fast 2-second test window.\n- [ ] One real Git above-floor transfer remains a non-stall failure across the production 10-second window.\n- [ ] Deterministic argv tests prove every wrapper still installs the shared low-speed options.\n- [ ] git diff origin/main -- src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py is empty and the full default suite passes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe original full suite passed 11,881 tests before one dribble failure. The cumulative-only attempt passed 13 focused tests but a second full suite passed 11,852 tests before another dribble failure, proving catch-up alone is insufficient.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/_stall_remote.py","reason":"Make dribble pacing cumulative-time based so delayed wake-ups catch up instead of lowering delivered throughput."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_network_fetch_stall_abort_851e.py","reason":"Add deterministic pacing regression coverage and verify all three shared-fixture fetch surfaces."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4.py","reason":"Verify the second consumer stall and dribble cases retain the shared fixture contract."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e9f459dd-e92c-41b2-a517-546b34f57e73","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["test","flake","network"],"ticket_id":"62d7-66d5-9301-4364","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Dribbling git-fetch test flakes under full-suite scheduler load","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f2043a8f-2611-480a-913a-da2ff1512e28","614919e9-5f1f-4faf-8a81-d0fb0bedfac1","8816eff1-41c4-48c1-8ddf-1f0d880c3b5d","de911254-faa6-47c2-80a1-06cbd2ee76ed","2438cf77-2176-48ec-9a28-e7a27edc1bd4","276b1093-4e38-439f-8573-a619d01c4578","939a2c32-4f41-474f-a4bf-4819d1f5c923","e9f459dd-e92c-41b2-a517-546b34f57e73","b5068a92-029c-4459-85a8-b94e00677bc2","3bde9d8b-2f6c-45b9-a996-3e712b817da4","4b958e28-b881-4b78-a3e0-0b574d606ba4","689d2d8a-07ad-45b1-8989-0660404c10e6","111708ec-0eb2-4f22-a1f4-e7a2eec57892"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786452161492595002,"uuid":"e8b34319-bea4-4c59-ab82-268bdd0fbaa1"}